# Tailwind CSS Styling

Styling uses Tailwind CSS via `@colorye/react-native-css` with the `className` prop.

## Usage

```tsx
<View className="flex-row items-center justify-between gap-2 rounded-md bg-gray-25 p-4">
  <Text className="text-lg font-bold text-primary">Title</Text>
</View>
```

## Conditional Classes

Use `cx` from `clsx`:

```tsx
import cx from "clsx";

<Text className={cx("text-lg font-bold", {
  "text-green-500": value >= 0,
  "text-red-500": value < 0,
})} />
```

## Color Palette

- `primary` (#FFB225 HVA / #FFE555 Mofi), `success` (#12B76A), `warning` (#FFB700), `danger`/`error` (#E01818)
- `gray-{25,50,100,200,300,500,700,900}` -- 25 is lightest background, 900 is near-black
- `yellow-{50..900}`, `green-{50,500,700}`, `red-{50,500,700}`, `blue-{50,500,700}`, `orange-{50,500,700}`

## Font Utilities

- `font-light`, `font-normal` (Manrope-Regular), `font-medium`, `font-semibold`, `font-bold`, `font-extrabold`, `font-black` (all Manrope family)
- `font-nasalization` (NasalizationRg), `font-times`, `font-times-bold`

## Font Sizes

- `text-2xs` (10px), `text-xs`/`text-base` (12px), `text-sm` (14px), `text-md` (16px), `text-lg` (18px), `text-xl` (20px), `text-2xl` (26px), `text-3xl` (30px)

## Rules

- Always prefer `className` over inline `style={{}}`
- Use `__combinedStyles` prop when applying className to raw RN primitives (Pressable, etc.)
- Only use inline `style` for truly dynamic values that can't be expressed as Tailwind classes
